{
  "rationale": "This is iteration 0, so there is no race telemetry or integration feedback yet. I am starting from a symmetric, conservative baseline. Five sensors span about 4 cm across the 25 mm tape, at x = -0.02 to +0.02 m, so the line stays visible across small lateral errors. They sit 5 cm ahead of the axle, which gives look-ahead for bends. The weights are proportional to sensor x (-2 to +2), so the signal is roughly the line's lateral offset in sensor units. A 0.10 m body keeps the off-track limit at its 0.06 m floor. Wheel track 0.12 m and radius 0.03 m give a moderate turn authority. Mass 0.6 kg keeps inertia low for quick acceleration toward the roughly 1.5 m/s average needed to finish within 3 s. I expect this to complete the oval and s-bend with few line losses. The main unknowns are whether the 1.5 base speed is too fast for the bends and whether the sensor spacing is too coarse for the slalom.",
  "geometry": {
    "sensor_positions": [
      {"x": -0.02, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": -0.01, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.0, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.01, "y": 0.05},
      {"x": 0.02, "y": 0.05}
    ],
    "sensor_size": 0.012,
    "wheel_track": 0.12,
    "wheel_radius": 0.03,
    "body_width": 0.10,
    "body_length": 0.16,
    "mass": 0.6
  },
  "intent": "Baseline symmetric five-sensor array with forward look-ahead and moderate wheel track, paired with a moderate-speed controller. The purpose is to get a clean reference race. I expect completion on the development tracks, with line_loss_events near 0 and rms_error under about 0.03 m. The array's ability to resolve the line should be tested first; if the Integrator reports saturation or oscillation, I will widen the spacing or move the sensors.",
  "feedback_request": {
    "questions": [
      "Does the five-sensor array at 0.01 m spacing give a clean, non-saturating signal on the tape at the 1.5 base speed?",
      "Is kp and kd within a stable range, or is there oscillation on the s-bend and slalom?",
      "Does the base speed of 1.5 cause the robot to leave the track in sharp bends, or does it finish comfortably?",
      "Is there any reason to change sensor_weights from the proportional-to-x pattern?"
    ],
    "integration_notes_wanted": "Please report the controller values you needed and any geometry changes you would have liked, with the reason for each."
  },
  "learning": "Baseline only: no evidence yet. Next iteration, adjust sensor spacing, lookahead y, and mass based on the race's rms_error, steering_oscillation, and line_loss_events."
}
